augb:{"n":"Augustinus Broesder","d":"1904– · Nieuwolda","s":"b","p":["tjaardj","antje"],"r":["nl"],"b":1904,"t":"Born at Nieuwolda on 2 February 1904, when his father was the village baker. He followed the trade and was a baker when he married Aaltje Steringa, a blacksmith's daughter from Eelde, on 24 April 1930; by then his father kept the café in Zuidlaren.","src":[["Open Archives: Augustinus Broesder","https://www.openarchieven.nl/search.php?lang=en&name=Augustinus+Broesder"]]},
roelfienb:{"n":"Roelfien Antje Broesder","d":"1899– · Nieuwolda","s":"b","p":["tjaardj","antje"],"r":["nl"],"b":1899,"t":"Born at Nieuwolda on 2 April 1899, the baker's daughter. She married Jacobus Mennen, a gardener from Oude Pekela, at Zuidlaren on 22 August 1928, when her father was the café keeper there. Jacobus died at Zuidlaren in 1969.","src":[["Open Archives: Roelfien Antje Broesder","https://www.openarchieven.nl/search.php?lang=en&name=Roelfien+Antje+Broesder"]]},
edwardaf:{n:'Edward Anthony Frankish',sn:'Ted Frankish',d:'1935–1974 · Narembeen',b:1935,x:1974,s:'f',p:['walter','mona'],r:['au'],t:'Known as Ted. Born at Narembeen Private Hospital, in the WA wheatbelt, on 17 January 1935, while the family home was at Gallipoli Street, Victoria Park; his middle name, Anthony, was his grandmother Matilda\'s maiden name. He moved to Melbourne with his parents in 1952 or 1953, and died in 1974.',src:[['Birth notice, West Australian, 19 Jan 1935','https://trove.nla.gov.au/newspaper/article/32847485']]},
walterwf:{n:'Walter Wetherall Frankish',d:'m. 1962',s:'f',p:['walter','mona'],r:['au']},
romona:{"n": "Ramona Frankish", "sn": "Ramona (Romona) Frankish", "d": "b. 1932 · Scarborough, WA", "b": 1932, "s": "f", "p": ["walter", "mona"], "r": ["au"], "ch": "frankish", "t": "Walter and Mona’s only daughter, born at the family home at Scarborough Beach on 6 December 1932. Known in the family as Romona; the Perth papers spell her Ramona. In May 1941, when the family lived at Victoria Park, her uncle Private E. A. Fisk, Mona’s brother, wrote to her from the Middle East with the AIF about his leave in Jerusalem and Bethlehem, and the Daily News printed his letter. In 1949 and 1950 she was one of the mannequins in Perth fashion parades. She moved to Melbourne with her parents in 1952 or 1953.", "src": [["Letter from Private E. A. Fisk, Daily News (Perth), 27 May 1941", "https://trove.nla.gov.au/newspaper/article/83021295"], ["Fashion parade, West Australian, 24 Mar 1950", "https://trove.nla.gov.au/newspaper/article/47837258"], ["Death notices for Jesse Frankish, West Australian, 27 Dec 1948", "https://trove.nla.gov.au/newspaper/article/47633969"]]},
robertwf:{"n":"Robert Wetherall Frankish","d":"1892–1973 · Hull","b":1892,"x":1973,"s":"f","p":["thomas2","emily"],"r":["uk","au"],"t":"Born in Hull in 1892 and brought to Western Australia as a small boy, landing at Albany with his mother in 1897. He stayed in Northam, married Nora McDermott in 1915, and lived in West Northam, later in Lockyer Avenue. He was active in the Labor Party's Avon Valley district council by 1930, and from 1945 sat on Northam Municipal Council for the West Ward, retiring for health reasons at the end of 1948 and then being returned unopposed for another vacancy a week later. In September 1943 he and Nora were told that their eldest son, Flight Sergeant Robert Walter Frankish, had been killed in an aircraft accident in England. He died at Northam in 1973, aged 80.","src":[["Northam Advertiser, 25 Sep 1943","https://nla.gov.au/nla.news-article260330520"],["Northam Advertiser, 3 Dec 1948","https://nla.gov.au/nla.news-article211929962"],["Northam Advertiser, 10 Dec 1948","https://nla.gov.au/nla.news-article211930318"],["Northam Advertiser, 12 Feb 1930","https://nla.gov.au/nla.news-article260227226"]]},
raaf:{"n":"Robert Walter Wetherall Frankish","d":"1916–1943","b":1916,"x":1943,"s":"f","p":["robertwf",null],"r":["au","uk"],"t":"Lawrie's first cousin, the eldest son of Robert and Nora Frankish of Northam. A Flight Sergeant in the RAAF, he had been in England about a year and was in command of a medium bomber when he was killed in an aircraft accident on 18 September 1943, aged 27. He is buried at Harrogate in Yorkshire, not far from the Marston farm country his grandmother Emily came from.","src":[["Northam Advertiser, 25 Sep 1943","https://nla.gov.au/nla.news-article260330520"]]},
margaret:{n:'Margaret Elaine Brazier',d:'b. 1932',b:1932,s:'y',p:['bruce','aileen'],r:['png','au'],img:'img/debutantes-1951.jpg',ch:'guinea',t:'Born in 1932, the elder daughter, while the family lived in the Territory of New Guinea. In November 1951 she made her debut at the Michaelmas Ball in Port Moresby, one of five debutantes photographed for Pacific Islands Monthly. In February 1956 she was visiting her grandmother at Hendra with her mother before they went back to Port Moresby.',src:[['Port Moresby Debutantes, PIM, 1 Nov 1951','https://nla.gov.au/nla.obj-331027255'],['Port Moresby Has City Comforts, Telegraph, 11 Feb 1956','https://trove.nla.gov.au/newspaper/article/293831648']]},
brucew:{n:'Bruce Warwick Brazier',d:'1941–2006',b:1941,x:2006,s:'y',p:['bruce','aileen'],r:['png','au'],t:'Born in 1941. He was a baby when his mother brought the three children south in the December 1941 evacuation; he landed at Brisbane from the Bulolo on 2 January 1951, aged nine, and by 1956 was boarding at Churchie. Died on 24 April 2006 aged 64, late of Indooroopilly.'},
charlesw:{n:'Charles Elliott Webb',d:'jeweller, Prahran',s:'p',p:['elliott','marthah'],r:['au'],t:'A jeweller and watchmaker in Greville Street, Prahran, who made the family brooch for his sister Mabel.'},
elsie:{n:'Elsie Alice Smith',d:'b. 1905 · Prahran',b:1905,s:'p',p:['ern','mabel'],r:['au'],t:'Born in Prahran on 20 June 1905. She married Donald Frederick George Parkinson, Ben\'s brother, at Hoddles Creek on 27 January 1934.'},
